<div class="section" id="market-scenario">
  <div class="page-wrap">
    <div class="section-label">01 · Market Scenario</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">The Current State of India's Ecommerce Seller Market</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">
      India's marketplace seller ecosystem is undergoing rapid professionalisation. The low-barrier entry window that Meesho created is now producing a second wave — sellers who tried, struggled, and are now actively seeking structured guidance. This is precisely the market you're positioned to serve.
    </p>

    <div class="stat-row">
      <div class="stat-pill">
        <span class="num">5M+</span>
        <span class="lbl">Active & Aspiring Sellers<br>Across Indian Marketplaces</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-pill">
        <span class="num">₹1,500Cr</span>
        <span class="lbl">Est. Seller Education Market<br>India (2026 projection)</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-pill">
        <span class="num">25–30%</span>
        <span class="lbl">YoY Growth in Online<br>Seller Coaching Demand</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-pill">
        <span class="num">₹400B</span>
        <span class="lbl">India E-commerce<br>Market Size (2025)</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid-2">
      <div class="card card-teal">
        <h3>What's Fuelling Demand for Coaching</h3>
        <p>Meesho's 213M+ annual transacting users and Flipkart's 1.4M+ seller base represent a massive top-of-funnel for education. Every new seller who faces their first RTO spike, account penalty, or zero-order week becomes a potential coaching buyer. Platform complexity is increasing — which makes professional guidance more valuable, not less.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card card-coral">
        <h3>The Free Content Overhang Problem</h3>
        <p>YouTube in Hindi carries thousands of hours of free seller content. This creates a floor of "informed but stuck" buyers — they know the theory but haven't cracked execution. Your paid program must justify its premium on <strong style="color:var(--text)">speed, curation, community, or proven outcomes</strong> — not information alone. Generic course content is a commodity. Outcomes are not.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="notice-box" style="margin-top:24px;">
      <strong>Market Maturity Reading:</strong> This market is at Stage 2–3 of the Eugene Schwartz awareness curve for the majority of the target audience. Most potential buyers are <em>problem-aware but not solution-aware</em> — they know they're struggling but don't yet know structured ecom coaching exists as a solution. This has direct implications for your ad creative strategy covered in Section 6.
    </div>

    <div class="grid-3" style="margin-top:28px;">
      <div class="card">
        <div style="margin-bottom:10px;"><span class="badge badge-green">Tailwind</span></div>
        <h3>AI Integration Gap</h3>
        <p>Less than 10% of Indian ecom courses currently include structured AI tooling modules. Your Module 27 is a legitimate differentiator — for now. That window is roughly 12–18 months before competitors catch up.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div style="margin-bottom:10px;"><span class="badge badge-amber">Headwind</span></div>
        <h3>Commoditised Messaging</h3>
        <p>"2026 updated" and "ghar baithe kamao" frameworks are saturated. Every competing creator is running the same narrative. Standing out requires a specific, evidence-backed promise — not more content.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div style="margin-bottom:10px;"><span class="badge badge-teal">Opportunity</span></div>
        <h3>Platform Professionalisation</h3>
        <p>Meesho, Flipkart, and Amazon are raising quality bars, penalising low-quality sellers, and tightening account rules. This turns professional training from "nice to have" into a risk management tool.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- SECTION 2: COMPETITION -->
