      Before scaling Meta ads, Sahil, these are the foundational things we need locked in. Running ads on a poorly positioned offer is expensive. Building these assets first dramatically reduces cost per acquisition and ensures the funnel actually converts at scale.
    </p>

    <div class="step-item">
      <div class="step-num">1</div>
      <div class="step-content">
        <h4>Reframe the Offer — Stop Selling a Course, Start Selling a System</h4>
        <p>The current framing is "Ecommerce Seller Mastery 2026 — a course." This is how every competitor is positioned. The shift needed: <mark>position the offer as a complete selling system with a specific outcome promise</mark>. Example: "The Marketplace Selling System: Go from ₹0 to your first ₹50,000/month on Meesho, Flipkart, or Amazon — with a step-by-step framework and AI tools that work in 2026." The word "system" implies structure and predictability. The specific revenue number makes it concrete. This alone changes how cold traffic reads the ad and the landing page.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-item">
      <div class="step-num">2</div>
      <div class="step-content">
        <h4>Set a Defensible Price at ₹3,499 — Not ₹999 or ₹1,999</h4>
        <p>There is a temptation to price low to generate volume. Resist it. Low pricing signals low value in a market where free content already exists. A ₹3,499 price point, justified by the AI module, 800+ product lists, 28 structured modules, and a money-back guarantee, positions the course as a premium product in a commodity market. It also makes the unit economics of Meta ads viable — at ₹999, you need a ROAS of 5x+ just to break even. At ₹3,499, a ROAS of 2x is profitable. For the first challenge launch, a ₹2,999 early-bird price is acceptable to generate momentum and reviews.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-item">
      <div class="step-num">3</div>
      <div class="step-content">
        <h4>Differentiate on AI — Make It a Front-Door Feature, Not a Bonus Module</h4>
        <p>Module 27 exists in your course as an add-on. The market research shows this is the single most underutilised differentiator in the India ecom coaching space. The offer should be repositioned as <mark>India's first AI-powered ecommerce seller system</mark>. This means putting AI front and centre in: the course name/subtitle, the landing page headline, ad creatives, and the course experience itself. Show students using AI for product research, listing writing, and ad optimisation — and make that the promise. This creates a moat that traditional "teach-and-record" competitors cannot easily replicate.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
